model {
  extend basalt.toolsGateway {
    metadata {
      constraint "The dashboard's built server render never highlights code: its server build swaps the code highlighter for an engine that reports it unavailable, so Shiki stays out of the dashboard Worker's upload and server-rendered code views are plain text. A page load therefore shows its code blocks plain until the browser's engine loads and colors them; before the swap the server sent them colored, and hydration kept those colors because each line holds the same text. A dev server still highlights on the server. The server build fails if it no longer swaps the engine; production upload checks reject the highlighter in the dashboard upload, refuse a chunk they cannot read, and require the highlighter in the browser build. Worker upload and startup budgets stay unchanged."
    }
  }
}
